[h1]Glorp UI — Societal Value Hints[/h1]

An add-on for Glorp UI. Hover a societal value and the tooltip tells you what pushes it further in that direction. This mod fills that list in, and drops from it what your country cannot take.

[b]What it does[/b]
[list]
[*] Glorp UI's own hint list in all eleven game languages. In everything except English it used to render empty.
[*] A second block with the sources Glorp UI's list does not cover: buildings, religious aspects and schools, employment systems, parliament issues, cabinet actions, international organizations, advances, missions, subject types, estates and chivalric orders — plus the standing modifiers that grow with your country (fort maintenance, average control, literacy, estate shares) and the conditional ones (war, bankruptcy, the fort limit).
[*] A third block for what is out of reach today but not out of reach forever.
[*] Availability filtering: an aspect of another religion, an organization you cannot join, a mission in a game with missions switched off — none of it is shown. Can be switched off in the Community Mod Framework mod menu.
[/list]

[b]Requires[/b]
[list]
[*] Glorp UI
[*] Community Mod Framework
[/list]
Load it after Glorp UI. The launcher does that on its own.

[b]Languages[/b]
English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, Türkçe, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어

[b]Compatibility[/b]
Overrides Glorp UI's two societal value tooltip templates. Another mod that changes the same templates will conflict.

[hr][/hr]
[i]This mod, including this description, was made with the help of an AI. It has been tested as far as I was able to, and I am satisfied with the result.[/i]
